## Why This Is Asked
Beginner DP concepts with a new angle: counting unordered combinations (coin change ways) and contrasting memoization with tabulation.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic programming (top-down memoization)
- Tabulation (bottom-up DP)
- Unordered combinations vs permutations
- Space optimization (1D DP)

## Code Example
```javascript
function countWaysTopDown(coins, target) {
  const n = coins.length;
  const memo = new Map();
  function dfs(i, rem) {
    if (rem === 0) return 1;
    if (rem < 0 || i === n) return 0;
    const key = i + '|' + rem;
    if (memo.has(key)) return memo.get(key);
    const res = dfs(i + 1, rem) + dfs(i, rem - coins[i]);
    memo.set(key, res);
    return res;
  }
  return dfs(0, target);
}

function countWaysBottomUp(coins, target) {
  const dp = new Array(target + 1).fill(0);
  dp[0] = 1;
  for (const c of coins) {
    for (let r = c; r <= target; r++) {
      dp[r] += dp[r - c];
    }
  }
  return dp[target];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you count permutations (order matters) instead of combinations?
- How would you handle very large targets or mod results to avoid overflow in languages with fixed integer sizes?

Why This Is Asked
- Tests dynamic augmentation of a trie with aggregated metrics and tie-breaking logic.

Key Concepts
- Trie augmentation with subtreeSum and subtreeBest; O(length) updates; O(length) queries.
- Correct handling of weight deltas, insertions, and removals; lexicographic tiebreaks.

Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = new Map();
    this.subtreeSum = 0;
    this.bestWord = null;
    this.bestWeight = 0;
  }
}
class DynamicDict {
  constructor() {
    this.root = new TrieNode();
    this.wordWeights = new Map();
  }
  add(word, delta) {
    let node = this.root;
    const newWeight = (this.wordWeights.get(word) || 0) + delta;
    this.wordWeights.set(word, newWeight);
    for (const char of word) {
      if (!node.children.has(char)) {
        node.children.set(char, new TrieNode());
      }
      node = node.children.get(char);
      node.subtreeSum += delta;
      if (newWeight > node.bestWeight || 
          (newWeight === node.bestWeight && word < node.bestWord)) {
        node.bestWord = word;
        node.bestWeight = newWeight;
      }
    }
  }
  query(prefix) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of prefix) {
      if (!node.children.has(char)) {
        return [0, null];
      }
      node = node.children.get(char);
    }
    return [node.subtreeSum, node.bestWord];
  }
}
```

Complexity Analysis
- `add(word, delta)`: O(|word|) time, O(1) extra space per character
- `query(prefix)`: O(|prefix|) time, O(1) extra space

Edge Cases
- Negative deltas potentially removing words completely
- Multiple words with equal maximum weights requiring lexicographic tie-breaking
- Empty queries and non-existent prefixes
- Words sharing common prefixes affecting aggregate calculations

